course: dictionary
lesson: 5091
title: Many meanings: intend
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Intend is one of these words. «I intend to finish my homework tonight» means I plan to do it. The words around it show the meaning.
explain: Look at a second meaning: «This gift is intended for you.» Here intend means the gift is meant to be for you. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a plan, or about who something is for? That question helps you pick the right meaning.
explain: Stories often use intend to show a plan that goes wrong. A character intends to do something, but things do not turn out as hoped. Watch for phrases like «did not intend» and «as intended», which show whether a plan worked out.
fact: Intend means to plan or mean to do something.
fact: Intend can also mean that something is meant to be for a certain person or use, as in «This gift is intended for you.»
fact: Intend can mean the meaning you give to your words, as in «What did you intend by that remark?»
fact: Useful phrases: intend to do, be intended for, did not intend, as intended.
fact: Intended is the past form: «I intended to finish my homework.»
exercise: «I intend to finish my homework tonight.» What does intend mean here? | To be given to someone as a gift | To feel tired after school | To shout loudly | *To plan to do something
exercise: «This gift is intended for you.» What does intended mean here? | Very large | *Meant to be for you | Wrapped in paper | Lost on the way home
exercise: «The rescue went as intended.» What does as intended mean? | Very quickly | By accident | Without any help | *The way it was planned
test: «She did not intend to break the vase.» What does this tell you? | *She did not plan to break it, so it was an accident | She broke it on purpose | She was sad about the vase | She planned to break it
test: «You intended to harm me, but God intended it for good.» In the first part, intended to harm means | *Planned to hurt someone | Forgot to do something | Was asked to sing | Wished to help someone
exam: A bottle says «intended for adults only». What does it mean? | Children may use it with a grown-up | Adults must pay for it | It is made of glass | *Only adults should use it
